# Code generated by Claude
"""
Demo: the solver can switch to a different arm solution (a "snap" / "branch jump").

Near a straight elbow, giving the solver an arm pose (as S, E, W points plus a wrist
rotation) can return DIFFERENT joint angles whose wrist point is centimetres away
from the commanded one: joints 3 and 5 jump by up to ~1.6 rad in one step, even
with the collision filter OFF. This is the IK, not the filter. This script shows it.

    # scenario 1 (default): drive an arm toward a config that failed to round-trip
    python experiments/branch_jump_demo.py                  # biggest failure, 5 s
    python experiments/branch_jump_demo.py --index 3        # another failing config
    python experiments/branch_jump_demo.py --list           # just list the failures
    python experiments/branch_jump_demo.py --video          # also render an MP4

    # scenario 2: a realistic motion, reaching forward at shoulder height
    python experiments/branch_jump_demo.py --scenario reach --video
    python experiments/branch_jump_demo.py --scenario reach --arm right --video

What it does (headless, kinematic, no viewer)
  * models/policies/branch_jump_policy.py moves one arm in joint space from a start
    pose to a target (failure scenario: the solver's default pose to a failing config
    over --duration s, linear; reach scenario: a natural pose with the elbow bent
    90 degrees to a full forward reach at shoulder height over 4 s, smooth, then hold 2 s).
  * At every 750 Hz sim step the commanded joints go through src/safety_filter.py twice:
    filter ON (the real case) and OFF (control). The solver is streamed (not reset).
  * A jump is a step where an output joint moves by more than --jump-threshold
    (default 0.1 rad) while the command moves ~0.001 rad. Prints its time, the joints,
    the size and the implied joint speed, and the wrist gap (3D distance between the
    commanded wrist point and the solver output's wrist point, from robot_fk_at).
  * Reach scenario only: checks the motion against the joint limits and for
    self-collision (MuJoCo contacts on Kong's bimanual model, commanded and filtered).
  * Saves data/branch_jump/trajectory.csv and trajectory.png (reach scenario:
    reach_trajectory.csv / reach_trajectory.png).
  * --video: physics with the PD controller tracking the FILTERED output (base held
    still, motor torque limits applied), rendered offscreen with EGL.
      failure scenario: data/branch_jump/branch_jump.mp4
      reach scenario:   data/branch_jump/reach_forward.mp4 (side view; two markers on
        the hand, orange = commanded, blue = actual; slow motion around the snap) and
        stills reach_before.png / reach_after.png.
"""

